# Declared fixture branches:  <branch><TAB><reason>
#
# A fixture branch exists to CARRY a defect — a breaking change an experiment has
# to measure, a broken tree a gate has to be proved against. Gating it is
# meaningless: it cannot pass a check designed to stop the very thing it exists
# for, and re-running the review will never change that.
#
# This is the only way past the gate that does not need a person at a terminal,
# and it is deliberately narrow:
#   - the branch must be the one currently checked out, matched in full, no globs
#   - the list is read from origin/main, NOT the working tree: a branch cannot add
#     its own name and push in the same breath. An entry counts once it is merged
#   - a reason of only whitespace does not count
#   - it lives in git, so adding a branch is a reviewable change somebody approved,
#     not an environment variable nobody sees
#   - the reason is echoed on every push, so it cannot be forgotten
#
# A fixture branch is never for merging. Delete its line once the branch is gone.

demo/breaking-api-change	carries the breaking change the with/without-skills experiment measures; never to be merged
